<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan depreciates rupee against dollar.</title>
<headline>Pakistan depreciates rupee against dollar.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan (SBP) depreciated the rupee on Thursday to 35.6200/35.8337 to the dollar from 35.5300/35.7077 fixed on August 13, the bank said.  </p>
<p>The bank gave no reason for the depreciation, the latest in a series carried out under the central bank's &quot;crawling peg&quot; management of the embattled local currency.</p>
<p>The rupee has fallen 0.85 percent this month and 1.48 percent since July 1, the start of fiscal 1996/97. It has lost four percent of its dollar value since January 1.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
